{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useNavigate"},{"type":"text","value":" hook is a hook that returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"navigate"},{"type":"text","value":" function that can be used to navigate to a new location. This includes changes to the pathname, search params, hash, and location state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usenavigate-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useNavigate options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useNavigate"},{"type":"text","value":" hook accepts a single argument, an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"opts-from-option","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opts.from"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description: The location to navigate from. This is useful when you want to navigate to a new location from a specific location, rather than the current location."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usenavigate-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useNavigate returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"navigate"},{"type":"text","value":" function that can be used to navigate to a new location."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"navigate-function","children":[{"type":"text","value":"navigate function"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"navigate"},{"type":"text","value":" function is a function that can be used to navigate to a new location."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"navigate-function-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"navigate function options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"navigate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a single argument, an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"link","href":"./NavigateOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NavigateOptions"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"navigate-function-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"navigate function returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":" that resolves when the navigation is complete"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate({ from: '/posts' })\n  const handleClick = () => navigate({ search: { page: 2 } })\n  // ...\n}\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            search: { page: 2 },\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (Page 2)\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            hash: 'my-hash',\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (Hash)\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            state: { from: 'home' },\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (State)\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"usenavigate-options","text":"useNavigate options","level":2},{"id":"opts-from-option","text":"opts.from option","level":3},{"id":"usenavigate-returns","text":"useNavigate returns","level":2},{"id":"navigate-function","text":"navigate function","level":2},{"id":"navigate-function-options","text":"navigate function options","level":3},{"id":"navigate-function-returns","text":"navigate function returns","level":3},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `useNavigate` hook is a hook that returns a `navigate` function that can be used to navigate to a new location. This includes changes to the pathname, search params, hash, and location state.\n\n## useNavigate options\n\nThe `useNavigate` hook accepts a single argument, an `options` object.\n\n### `opts.from` option\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Optional\n- Description: The location to navigate from. This is useful when you want to navigate to a new location from a specific location, rather than the current location.\n\n## useNavigate returns\n\n- A `navigate` function that can be used to navigate to a new location.\n\n## navigate function\n\nThe `navigate` function is a function that can be used to navigate to a new location.\n\n### navigate function options\n\nThe `navigate` function accepts a single argument, an `options` object.\n\n- Type: [`NavigateOptions`](./NavigateOptionsType.md)\n\n### navigate function returns\n\n- A `Promise` that resolves when the navigation is complete\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate({ from: '/posts' })\n  const handleClick = () => navigate({ search: { page: 2 } })\n  // ...\n}\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            search: { page: 2 },\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (Page 2)\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            hash: 'my-hash',\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (Hash)\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            state: { from: 'home' },\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (State)\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useNavigateHook\ntitle: useNavigate hook\n---\n\nThe `useNavigate` hook is a hook that returns a `navigate` function that can be used to navigate to a new location. This includes changes to the pathname, search params, hash, and location state.\n\n## useNavigate options\n\nThe `useNavigate` hook accepts a single argument, an `options` object.\n\n### `opts.from` option\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Optional\n- Description: The location to navigate from. This is useful when you want to navigate to a new location from a specific location, rather than the current location.\n\n## useNavigate returns\n\n- A `navigate` function that can be used to navigate to a new location.\n\n## navigate function\n\nThe `navigate` function is a function that can be used to navigate to a new location.\n\n### navigate function options\n\nThe `navigate` function accepts a single argument, an `options` object.\n\n- Type: [`NavigateOptions`](./NavigateOptionsType.md)\n\n### navigate function returns\n\n- A `Promise` that resolves when the navigation is complete\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate({ from: '/posts' })\n  const handleClick = () => navigate({ search: { page: 2 } })\n  // ...\n}\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            search: { page: 2 },\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (Page 2)\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            hash: 'my-hash',\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (Hash)\n      </button>\n      <button\n        onClick={() =>\n          navigate({\n            to: '/posts',\n            state: { from: 'home' },\n          })\n        }\n      >\n        Posts (State)\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
